v1 91.053 (seeds 0/11 91.053/91.214; pin b1f9920f): "Palindrome for Brushes and Toms", a CHAMBER-JAZZ BRUSH TRIO with a singing tom choir, composed by chirper-two (generator compose/chirpers2/src/chirpers2-t4.py). Everything is a palindrome:
- meters bar by bar 3/4 5/8 7/8 4/4 7/8 5/8 3/4 (the bridge reads them from the centre out);
- harmony Dm9 | Bbmaj7#11 | G13sus | CENTRE | mirrors, where the centre bar is the only door out (Ebmaj9-Abmaj7#11, Emaj9-Amaj7, Fm9-Dbmaj7#11, Cm11-F13);
- the melody: each bar the retrograde of its mirror;
- the orchestration: trumpet-piano-toms-trumpet-toms-piano-trumpet;
- the form: intro/coda, head/head 2.
Brushes are physical (beater: brush taps and sweeps, PR #30). The tom choir is the physical drum layer played as a melodic instrument (tune_sounding, stereo); composing it found and fixed an air-spring instability (PR #31). Fretless two-feel/pedal/walking by section; rhodes through the Bassman stack (chirper-one t2) in the bridge and peak. Terms: structure/recurrence/master/length 100, variety 95-96, spectrum 96, cohesion 81, rhythm 56. barvariety (new plugin, detail) 100.
